    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1272">

                <pb facs="1015" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/71.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Chargé d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-04T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Governor Colquitt of Texas, in a telegram received October 1, 1.15 p.m., replies
                    to Department’s September 30, as follows:</p>
                <p>[Telegram quoted.]</p>
                <p>You may bring the Governor’s suggested amendment of the Mexican Government’s
                    request to the attention of the Minister for Foreign <pb facs="1016" n="900"
                        xml:id="pg900"/> Affairs, unless you think it necessary for the Mexican
                    Government to make the next move, in view of representations you have already
                    made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
